<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  A launchd agent that starts the portal at login and restarts it if it stops.

    cp home-portal.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/lan.home.portal.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/lan.home.portal.plist

  Permissions. macOS asks the owner once before a process may reach the local network,
  removable volumes, the folders Documents, Desktop and Downloads, or other applications
  (Automation). The portal asks for all of them at start ([permissions] in the configuration)
  and lists the answers on Management > Permissions. Full Disk Access is never asked for;
  add home-portal in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Full Disk Access by hand when a
  script needs it.

  - Started from a terminal, the portal inherits the terminal's permissions: the prompts
    and the System Settings entries name the terminal app.
  - Started by this agent, the permissions belong to home-portal itself. macOS knows an
    unsigned binary by its contents, so a new build asks again: run the agent from an
    installed copy, and ask again after each upgrade.

  Ask and see the answers from the same context the portal runs in:  home-portal permissions
  Without Local Network every probe of a LAN address fails at once with the diagnosis
  "local-network-denied" instead of calling the service down; check with
  home-portal probe <service id>.

  Automations. Scripts from the scripts directory ([storage] in the configuration, scripts/
  beside it by default) run as the portal's user and
  inherit its permissions, all of the above included. launchd gives them a minimal PATH
  (/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin): call programs by their absolute path, or add a PATH
  entry to EnvironmentVariables below.

  Adjust the paths below to where the binary and the configuration live.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>lan.home.portal</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/local/bin/home-portal</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>HOME_PORTAL_CONFIG</key>
    <string>/Users/me/home-portal/home-portal.toml</string>
  </dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/me/home-portal</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/me/home-portal/portal.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/me/home-portal/portal.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
